    "explanation": "To the rider: your fare stands. To the driver: the diversion is excused.\n\nSame trip, and the excess is established. The trip record, GPS trace and fare ledger all carry trip_id TRP-00111 and the 07:47:40 start, so POL-RD-08(a) is met. On the governing distance — gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 29.98 km, not the rounded 30.0 km convenience copy on the trip record (POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern) — the trip ran 5.98 km / 24.92% over the booked 24.0 km optimal. That clears both establishment tests (over 0.8 km and over 20%), so a deviation is ESTABLISHED. It does not reach materiality (50% or 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile inquiry is triggered; in any event deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 588 completed trips, so no pattern exists.\n\nThe deviation is fully exonerated under POL-RD-03. LTA DataMall advisory ADV-20260803-014 (EV-ADVIS-00111-01) closed the PIE towards Tuas between Clementi Rd and Jalan Anak Bukit — the very segment the booked optimal route traverses — from 07:10 to 09:30, bracketing the 07:47–08:25 trip, and the trace shows the vehicle leaving the corridor at Bukit Panjang before the closed segment and rejoining after, which is the diversion the advisory itself directs. The exoneration cap is min(5.98, 1.30 x (29.2 - 24.0) + 1.00) = min(5.98, 7.76) = 5.98 km. The justified excess is therefore the whole of the measured excess, the closure-adjusted optimal is 24.0 + 5.98 = 29.98 km (37.5 minutes, being 30.0 min scaled by 29.98/24.0, the amended duration being null), and nothing is left to refund on distance.\n\nPOL-RD-02 run against the closure-adjusted optimal, as POL-RD-03 requires:\n- charged_total: SGD 37.74\n- recomputed_fare: SGD 37.585 — ((3.80 + 0.75 x 29.98 + 0.28 x 37.5) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, the only artifact carrying it) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP\n- refund: SGD 0.155, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so NO_ACTION.\n\nThe rider's alternative recomputation against the booked 24.0 km optimal (giving SGD 6.74) is not the computation the clause prescribes once POL-RD-03 excuses the excess, and is not adopted. The rider's assertion that she saw no closure cites no artifact, so under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight, and it is contradicted by a timestamped government advisory covering the disputed segment. The fare is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not close the distance route and POL-RD-02 is the operative remedy — but it produces no payable sum here. No POL-RD-05 re-quote exists (no amendment timestamps, amended_optimal_distance_km null), POL-RD-12 does not apply (vehicle_type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL), and POL-RD-04 is unavailable: the driver's 07:54:20 message was an announcement of the closure, the rider's only reply ('as long as i reach by 8.30') names no road and carries waypoint_hint null, so no rider-requested detour can be run. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: tolls_erp is 0.00 and erp_gantries is empty, so there is no pass-through or billing-integrity correction. The rider's profile (deviation_claims_60d of 1) does not engage the extra corroboration rule in POL-RD-08. Every artifact the ruling rests on — the trip record, the GPS trace and the traffic advisory — carries weight_multiplier 1.0, so no discount applies and the confidence floor is not approached. The outcome is NO_ACTION: the charge stands and no monetary sum moves.",
